
.TH PRINTENV 1 "October 2026" "printenv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
printenv \- print environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printenv
.RB [ \-0 ]
.RI [ VARIABLE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B printenv
prints the values of the specified environment variables.
.PP
If no variables are specified, the entire environment is
printed, with each entry in the form
.BR NAME=VALUE .
.PP
When one or more variable names are specified, only their
values are printed, in the order requested.
Variable names are not included in the output.
.PP
If a requested variable is not defined, no output is produced
for that variable, and the exit status is set to 1.
Processing continues with any remaining variables.
.PP
An environment variable with an empty value produces an
empty line and is considered defined.
.PP
By default, each output is terminated by a newline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
End each output with a NUL byte instead of a newline.
This allows safe processing of values containing newline
characters.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display all environment variables:
.PP
.RS
.B printenv
.RE
.PP
Display the value of a single variable:
.PP
.RS
.B printenv HOME
.RE
.PP
Example output:
.PP
.RS
.B /home/user
.RE
.PP
Display multiple variables:
.PP
.RS
.B printenv HOME USER SHELL
.RE
.PP
Example output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/home/user
user
/bin/bash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Produce NUL-terminated output:
.PP
.RS
.B printenv -0 PATH HOME
.RE
.PP
Test whether an environment variable is defined:
.PP
.RS
.nf
if printenv HOME > /dev/null; then
    echo "HOME is defined"
else
    echo "HOME is not defined"
fi
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion. All requested variables were found,
or the entire environment was printed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
One or more requested variables were not found or had
invalid names.
.TP
.B 2
An invalid option was specified or an output error occurred.
.SH STANDARDS
The basic functionality conforms to POSIX
.BR printenv .
The
.BR \-0 ,
.BR \-\-null ,
and
.B \-\-help
options are extensions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR env (1),
.BR export (1),
.BR getenv (3),
.BR environ (7)
